107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (Stock price modeling helps understand and predict price behaviors in different market contexts. This project applies Geometric Brownian Motion \(GBM\) and Ornstein-Uhlenbeck \(OU\) processes to model stock prices of Intel and AMD, two companies in the same industry, and Netflix, a company from a different industry, for comparison. By contrasting similar and different sectors, this analysis highlights how industry-specific and broader market dynamics influence stock price movements.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
